  "method": {
    "base_commit": "72b7023",
    "question": "Does avoiding the per-query planning SessionState clone reduce the remaining IN-table address variability?",
    "intervention": "One diagnostic benchmark executable. Both modes retain one native SessionState. Fresh uses the original DataFrame route; reuse calls mark_start_execution and create_physical_plan on the retained state after the unchanged Sail resolver. Generic-IN and subquery suites use the same helper. Execution TaskContext reuse is fixed in both modes.",
    "semantic_checks": "Preserve the native start-time, config snapshot and alias-generator refresh. Prepare timestamp queries and table-backed scalar subqueries, then execute in reverse to check statement-time and result isolation. Validate all existing 186 captures per state mode.",
    "design": "Two previously used native shared seed indices, 0 and 4, four processes for each fresh/reuse mode. Sorted resolver release, native allocator settings, fixed addresses, 32 warmups and 261 prepared plans. Reverse mode order for the second seed; use existing preparation and execution barriers.",
    "analysis": "Compare all hash and address traces. Require within-group and cross-mode hash controls for allocation interpretation. Timings and counters are retained but no performance effect is estimated.",
    "stopping_rule": "One diagnostic Rust build and exactly four groups. Retain every failure, capture and trace; no outcome-based extensions or input replacement. Validation precedes collection. No unrelated work overlaps collection; shared files are restored and hash-checked in finally.",
    "limits": [
      "Reuse applies only to this sequential read-only benchmark with fixed configuration and function registrations. It is not a production API proposal.",
      "Both modes retain an extra planning state; the fresh diagnostic is not byte-identical to the preceding executable.",
      "Physical subquery planning can still create its own owned state. This intervention does not remove every internal clone.",
      "The optional float type-inference patch stays unadopted. No claim of eliminated release cost or new Spark corpus coverage."
    ]
  },
